WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.560
ano toki umareta no

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.560
あのとき生まれたの

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.560
I'll softly give you my thoughts

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.070
watashi no omoi sotto ageru

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.070
私の想いそっとあげる

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.070
That were born at that moment

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.950
shinjite ite

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.950
信じていて

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.950
Please believe in them

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
deatta hi kara

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
出逢った日から

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.420
Since the day when we met

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.670
hajimete no kimochi megutteru

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.670
初めての気持ち巡ってる

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.670
For the first time, I have these feelings, and they go around

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
honto no egao hoshii nante

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
ホントの笑顔ほしいなんて

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.680
I want your true smile

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.560
anata ga oshiete kureta sorao

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.560
あなたが教えてくれた空を

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:42.560
I embrace the sky

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.690
dakishimete yume o miru

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.690
抱きしめて夢をみる

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:47.690
That you told me about and dream

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.520
tooi keredo・・・

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.520
遠いけれど・・・

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.520
It's faraway, but...

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.740
atatakai hikari no kakera

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.740
あたたかい光のかけら

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.740
The fragments of warm light

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.530
kizutsuita hane ni inochi o kureta no

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.530
傷ついた羽根に命をくれたの

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:00.530
Gave life to my wounded wings

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.950
fureta toki umareta

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.950
触れたとき生まれた

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.950
Born at the moment when we touched

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
tsuyoi watashi no soba ni

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
強い私のそばに

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.040
Next to me, who is strong

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.260
mamoraretai watashi ga nemutte ita no

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.260
守られたいわたしが眠っていたの

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.260
The me who wants to be protected was asleep

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.260
sou unmei kaerareru ne

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.260
そう運命変えられるね

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.260
That's right, destiny can be changed

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.310
futari no koi mezamesasete・・・

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.310
ふたりの恋目覚めさせて・・・

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:26.310
Let our love awaken...

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:29.900
{last frame of OP}

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:34.190
My body kind of feels dull,

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.740
and I thought it might be forgetting that feeling.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.410
Yes.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.740
Would Sunday at noon be okay?

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:45.950
Yes, right.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.500
Thank you.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.500
I'll call you again on Sunday.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:50.790
Yes.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:56.720
Fifth Episode 「Wish」

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:01.720
It's not like I <i>want</i> to see that woman named Yuuno.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.760
Just come with me for a bit.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.100
Can I go to your school and play again, then?

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.270
No way.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.140
This is a bargaining point.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.230
Where'd you learn that term?

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:12.940
On detective dramas.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.910
Everyone looks like they're having fun.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.740
That's because it's Sunday.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.250
Sunday?

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.960
People get to be with their families on Sunday, so that's why it's fun.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.340
Sunday is fun.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.960
It's fun because they're with their families.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:02:59.860
Shinkurou.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.580
We're not going to the Kuhouins', right?

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.160
Of course not.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:08.500
Really?

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.210
Really.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:13.080
I don't even know where that is.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.250
I see.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:18.920
Are the Kuhouins in a place with scenery like this too?

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.630
Well, that's fine.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.100
Shinkurou.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.390
Will you vow that you'll protect me?

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:35.270
What are you saying?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:39.530
Like, if that Yuuno woman attacks me or something.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.740
That wouldn't happen.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.030
This area is scary.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.700
And Yuuno knew about the Kuhouins.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.620
There's nothing scary.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.250
She's a really nice person too.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.230
Turtles.

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:18.690
I will go prepare some tea, so please wait here.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.860
Yes.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.170
It looks like my house, but it's kind of different.

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.380
Really?

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.500
Yes, it's interesting here.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.590
Did you see the turtles in the garden?

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:41.550
I did!

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.380
There's a bigger one over there.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.890
Welcome.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.180
Hello, Chi-chan.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.520
Who is this, Shinkurou?

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:55.270
Yuuno-san's sister, Chizuru-chan.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.520
Chi-chan, this is Murasaki.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.320
Try to be her friend, okay?

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.570
If you say so,

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.110
then I will.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.780
You're speaking too softly, and I can't hear you.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.490
If you have something to say, then don't hide and just say it.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:14.040
Hey, she's still young.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.250
How old are you?

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.160
She's five.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.120
What's your name?

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.250
Houzuki Chizuru.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.500
I'm asking this woman!

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:21.800
Woman?

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.130
Welcome.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.260
Hello.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.880
Welcome, you two.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.890
What do you think of this? It's newly made.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:32.760
Is that so?

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:33.770
That's a pretty color.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.180
Thank goodness.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:38.650
We've only been able to meet during school.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.860
Sorry, I just couldn't find the time to come.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:46.490
If you come here, then you can see me in these clothes anytime.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.780
You're right.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.120
Well, about this kimono, this pattern is-

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.870
Hey, Shinkurou.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.580
What? You need to go to the toilet?

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:56.370
No!

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.080
Maybe you're tired after coming such a long distance?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:01.460
I'm not tired.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.380
You don't need to go to the toilet, right?

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.210
I said no.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:07.720
All right then, Yuuno-san, let's go to the dojo.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:08.340
Sure.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.010
What are you going to do in the dojo?

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.600
What do you mean? We'll practice, of course.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.970
In that case, allow me to observe what this "practice" is.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.430
You'll be bored if you watch.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:16.310
Why's that?

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:18.140
It's not something a kid should see.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:20.060
Is it something perverted?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:21.480
That's completely wrong!

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.150
Really? They say women are monsters.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:27.440
Tamaki-san's teaching you more strange things.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:30.280
It wasn't Tamaki, it was on a suspense theatre!

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.740
You're watching too much TV.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.790
Is Murasaki-chan always like that?

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:42.580
She tends to believe what's on TV and what Yamie and Tamaki tell her.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:45.880
I told her to only watch TV for two hours.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.420
How about you buy her a game?

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.300
A game?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.140
Chi-chan is always playing games.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.970
Is that fun?

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.230
It is.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.440
It's not a TV, right?

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:01.310
Yeah.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.400
She's always playing the same game.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.570
She doesn't get bored of it?

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:09.900
You have to beat him?

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:10.570
Yeah.

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.320
So, he's a bad guy?

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:13.660
Yeah.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.030
Why are you an old man?

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.160
Because I chose him.

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:23.290
Please be careful, I'm a monster after all.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.170
Yes.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:28.090
Well then...

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.260
No, that's your ally.

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.560
He has a menacing face, though.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.020
If you don't block...

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:40.270
Be quiet!

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:41.770
Ah, watch out!

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:46.440
They attacked me from behind!

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:48.730
Looks like they don't know about chivalry!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.150
It's because you took out your ally.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:53.700
Ah, it'll break!

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:55.910
I can't lose to a game!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.910
Don't do that!

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.410
Just watch! I'll show you my-

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.420
Ah, it broke...

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.920
This...

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.630
It's too fragile.

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.510
It's not working.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.840
That's not fun at all.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.140
It broke...

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.470
Ah... I'm sorry.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:36.030
Your breathing is erratic because you don't defend properly.

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.750
I can see that you're trying to protect it.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.880
She can only hold the frying pan.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:53.420
It'll break.

00:08:53.420 --> 00:08:55.840
It can't possibly break that easily.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.560
This can be fixed easily.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.600
Don't worry, I can fix this!

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.980
They did the same thing on ER 24!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.980
The discomfort hasn't gone away yet, has it?

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.030
How should I say it...

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:14.740
Um...

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:17.740
Your body isn't familiar with it yet?

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:18.320
I...

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:23.330
I believe that not relying on it may be the best choice for me.

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.210
Do you regret having that put in you?

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.380
I wanted to become strong.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:33.760
I just wanted to become strong.

00:09:34.460 --> 00:09:37.340
But this is not true strength.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.550
I see...

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.850
That's why I will obtain true strength without relying on this.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.600
And what is true strength?

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:50.150
Strength of the mind.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:55.900
Just like when this was put in, I don't want to rely on other strengths.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:57.860
I want to use my own power.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:01.370
Let's begin again, then.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:02.870
Yes.

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:20.550
Look!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.490
I said I'll fix it!

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:41.530
Give it back!

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.010
Shinkurou!

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:07.470
Shinkurou?

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.240
He's got a more refined look now.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:30.830
He's become strong.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.630
Shinkurou...

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:44.840
You're as formal as ever. Let your legs loose.

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:45.800
Yes.

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:47.760
It's been a while, so how was your practice?

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:50.770
My body now knows how strict the Houzuki-ryuu is.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.520
How about having a spar with me some time?

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.520
I don't think I'll be much of a match with my current skills.

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:03.200
If you were so weak, then Benika wouldn't let you handle such troublesome jobs.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.530
I always make mistakes, though.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:12.330
That Yuuno is quite worried about the job you're currently involved with.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.210
It was a tougher practice than usual.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:22.920
When Yuuno is in the house, she unconsciously feels the pressure of being born into a family of killers.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:27.430
According to history, there are many tales

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:31.180
of the Houzuki family performing countless killings.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:35.770
In my generation, it was decided that that sort of killing would no longer be performed.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.570
We cannot let our powers and skills be lost though.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:46.070
Therefore, I have been given the responsibility to teach Yuuno and Chizuru the powers and skills of a killer.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:51.370
But then, as normal girls, they can't help but worry about you.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.410
That's...

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:55.540
Yuuno is able to be the most normal at school.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:59.000
So, how is she when she's there?

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:01.090
Can she smile from her heart?

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:04.470
Yes, I believe she has a wonderful smile.

00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.550
How was Yuuno's lunch?

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:10.510
You can be truthful. Was it bad?

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.680
Not at all! It was really good.

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:17.480
How boring, you're too serious of a man.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.350
No way...

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:22.150
I wonder what Yuuno finds so good about such a stiff man.

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:25.110
She always treats me nicely.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.700
You're like a relative to us, after all.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:33.450
You've been part of the family ever since you set foot in this house.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.540
Everyone is concerned for you.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:37.370
Thank you.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:40.000
You're so stiff, don't lower your head.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:53.220
She really looks like a kid when she's sleeping.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:56.810
She'd be a good girl if she were more obedient.

00:13:56.810 --> 00:13:59.900
You're becoming stronger in order to protect her, right?

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.570
There's that too.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:03.980
Hey.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:05.780
We're going home.

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:11.030
Well then...

00:14:11.030 --> 00:14:12.530
Take care.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:15.500
Sorry about your game, Chi-chan.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.410
I'll bring you a new one the next time I visit.

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.370
Yeah, make sure to come again.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:22.790
Come over any time, this is your home.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.380
Yes.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:25.710
Thank you.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:28.840
I'll walk with you to the station.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:30.550
It's all right.

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.220
It's okay.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.350
She's pretty heavy for a kid.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:41.560
That weight is what you imagine her weight to be.

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:45.570
There's also the weight of her existence and life.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.280
Yes.

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:53.370
I'm acting a bit too conceited, coming from a family of killers.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.280
That's not-

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:55.660
It is true.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:57.700
It is true...

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.370
I'm stained.

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:02.830
Let's stop this.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.630
I won't.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.210
You're scared of the Houzukis, aren't you?

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.220
They protected me.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.430
They made me stronger.

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:15.680
But the Houzukis have changed you.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.850
I just don't have to use it.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:25.190
I'll become stronger so I won't have to rely on this and become like Benika-san.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:28.230
For her sake and your own?

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:32.200
And for the Houzukis' sake, who raised me.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:34.950
I like you.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.660
I like all the Houzukis.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.250
I see.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:04.900
Hey, Murasaki.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.860
Is there anything you want to eat?

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.900
Hey, Murasaki.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.700
You're angry, aren't you?

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:13.950
About what?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.530
Um...

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:19.200
For breaking that woman Chizuru's doll.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.370
Ah, that.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.660
I fixed it.

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:25.000
You fixed it?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.040
Thank you.

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:30.000
I couldn't fix her game though, and it's expensive.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.510
I'll have to ask Benika-san to do something about it.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.880
The game that opens with a "clack?"

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:36.470
Ask her to get another one.

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:37.680
You want one?

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.470
It's a bargaining point for going to that house.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.310
It's expensive.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:44.310
I can't have one?

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.270
Do you want it that much?

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:47.730
I do.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:53.610
You can only play it for two hours a day.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:55.410
Yeah, I promise!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.410
You have to take care of it.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.450
I will!

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:58.830
I'll buy it for you then.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.280
Oh, yes!

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:01.120
What's with that?

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.580
Junko-san said to say that when you're happy!

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.080
TV again?

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.340
Are we going to eat this again?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:13.460
We always eat this, though.

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:15.340
Is there something else you want to eat?

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:17.640
Simmered mackerel with miso would be good.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.550
Simmered mackerel with miso?

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:21.390
That's quite a tasteful choice.

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:22.560
All right, it's decided, then.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:26.270
Wait, I don't know how to make it.

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:28.860
You first cut the mackerel with a knife.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:31.070
Put water, sake, soy, mirin, and sugar into the pan and let it simmer.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:33.070
Put the mackerel in with the skin facing up.

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:36.030
Cover the pan and let it simmer for 10 minutes at medium flame.

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:39.950
Remove the mackerel and then pour sauce from the pan and miso onto it.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:42.080
You then put it back in the pan to simmer and then it's complete.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.330
You can also serve it together with leek.

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:45.790
That's amazing.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.000
Did you learn that from the TV too?

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.120
That's right.

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.040
Learning things like that from the TV is good.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:53.590
If you don't eat the proper food, then there's no point in training your body.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:57.800
Some strangely tanned old man in the morning says, "I can't leave you alone!"

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:59.300
Who's that?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:04.430
It's a nice old man on the afternoon TV who listens to peoples' problems on the phone.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:06.680
That's fine to watch, then.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.310
He says, "I can't leave you alone!"

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:13.520
Murasaki!

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:21.660
Welcome back!

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:27.250
There are so many stupid couples on a nice day like this.

00:18:27.250 --> 00:18:31.000
I believe I'm a better woman, though.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.170
There seem to be traces of some massive binge drinking.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.800
We were waiting for you to come back, you know!

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:37.380
It stinks!

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.970
We wouldn't come in unless it was to drink.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.090
It's my room, though.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.300
I know!

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.510
I brought something really nice!

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:45.350
Are you listening?

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.140
I got it from my university.

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:48.600
What's that?

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.150
It warms up your room!

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.980
That's good! It's been cold in the mornings lately.

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:56.030
But it says that it's forbidden to take it.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:59.570
It's all right! We just need to take that off.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:00.740
Is it really okay?

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:03.910
Murasaki also says that this room is cold.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:04.580
That's right!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:05.910
You just need to wear thicker clothes!

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.370
That's a poverty-ridden way of thinking.

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:09.750
I <i>am</i> poor, though.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.790
The energy bill will be high, too!

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.670
Don't use it on warm days.

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:17.630
It's okay, you can just use it when he's at school.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:18.630
Tamaki-san!

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:20.130
Anyway, let's eat!

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.880
What's this dish called?

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.140
Boiled tofu.

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.510
Boiled tofu.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:26.140
It's good.

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:27.520
I want to try it!

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.480
Hold on.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:31.310
It's hot, so be careful.

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.480
Okay.

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:40.780
Is it good?

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:41.820
It's good!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:47.580
When summer comes, I'll get an air conditioner for you!

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.450
Please don't do that!

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:53.370
It's an old model, so you don't need to worry about it.

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.290
The energy bill will be high, though.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:57.090
Money, again?

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:00.510
Also, if you bring it here, who's going to install it?

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.720
That can be done easily.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:06.140
It's decided then! I'll bring back an air conditioner in the summer!

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.970
No, please don't just continue with the conversation!

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:11.270
We'll drink beer in an air-conditioned room all day!

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:12.850
That's the best.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.350
Does that mean you're going to hang out in my room?

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:18.520
So, where did you go today?

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:21.030
Please don't forcefully change the topic.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:23.280
Where did you go?

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:24.700
Nowhere, really.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:26.740
Sounds like you're hiding something big.

00:20:26.740 --> 00:20:28.490
Right?

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.580
What were you doing, and where?

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:33.000
I just took care of some business.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.710
And what kind of business was it?

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:36.460
We went to Yuuno's place.

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:38.460
Idi- Don't say anything!

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:41.880
Just what kind of business were you taking care of at your girlfriend's house?

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:43.050
It wasn't much.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.760
Were you taking care of "that?"

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:46.890
Why are you always thinking of those things?

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:51.720
Youth is made of sweat, tears, and overflowing juices!

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:53.270
What's this "overflowing juices?!"

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:54.690
I'm eating here.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:56.600
Did you go all the way to the home stretch?

00:20:56.600 --> 00:20:59.230
There's nothing between me and Yuuno-san!

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:01.320
They were practicing together by themselves.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.650
Idi- There you go again...

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:07.410
What kind of practice did you do alone together?

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:08.620
Just a normal practice.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:11.120
A normal "bed technique" practice, huh? {TLC}

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:13.080
Where are you getting this "bed" idea from?

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:14.710
If there're any "techniques" you don't know about,

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:18.420
you can come ask me anytime, okay?

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:20.210
Is there anything else to put in the pot?

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.710
It's boiled tofu, so there's only tofu.

00:21:22.710 --> 00:21:24.260
There's seaweed.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.470
That's soup stock, though.

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:27.430
There is something to put in!

00:21:30.600 --> 00:21:32.350
A week's worth of food expenses!

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:35.430
Hey, hey, don't be so cheap!

00:21:35.430 --> 00:21:36.100
But...

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:37.650
You sound so poor.

00:21:37.650 --> 00:21:38.980
I<i> am</i> poor!

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:42.610
Poor! Poor!

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:42.610
Sundays are really fun, after all.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:45.190
It's not funny!

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.830
It's getting cold.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:58.250
That looks delicious.

00:22:04.760 --> 00:22:07.300
I'm so lonely...

00:22:07.300 --> 00:22:09.800
I'm hungry...

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:11.550
This is good!

00:22:11.550 --> 00:22:13.510
It's soup stock! Soup stock!

00:22:13.510 --> 00:22:14.680
Where's the fish?

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:16.560
Eat up, Murasaki-chan!

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:17.640
Where's my fish?

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:19.100
Ladies first!

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:19.650
Where's the chicken?

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:21.520
Say "Aah," Murasaki-chan.

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:22.480
Aah!

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:23.480
Is that chicken?

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:24.530
It's good!

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:25.190
Where's mine?

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:27.320
Didn't you eat Yuuno-san?

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:28.280
I didn't!

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:29.740
You're talking in front of a kid, you know.

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:31.070
I'm underaged!

00:22:31.070 --> 00:22:32.830
Eat me too!

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:34.830
You're so mature, Murasaki!

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:34.830
Hey!

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:35.750
You can't say that!

00:22:35.750 --> 00:22:38.120
That's how an adult's conversation is.

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:39.830
It's not though!

00:23:00.690 --> 00:23:06.940
sonna ni asette sa nani mo kamo shiritai to omowanaide

00:23:00.690 --> 00:23:06.940
そんなに焦ってさ何もかも知りたいと思わないで

00:23:00.690 --> 00:23:06.940
Rushing so much, don't think that you want to know everything.

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:02.690
{last frame of Kimono}

